MINIPTERUS_assignment_02_genome_exploration
Name: BATIGULAO, JEHIAH BLESS T. 
Activity Title: Basic Genome Structure and Sequence Exploration Using Galaxy
BIO 300 – B Cell and Molecular Biology Laboratory
Species: Miniopterus schreibersii genome assembly (GCF_964146895.1)

Objectives
To describe the structure of a genome assembly using basic statistics, sequence-length analysis, length filtering, and a small-scale open reading frame (ORF) exploration, and to learn how to inspect and interpret an assembled genome.

 Tools used in Galaxy
Part 1 — Genome Identity
- Source: NCBI
- Assembly accession: GCF_964146895.1
- Assembly name: GCF_964146895.1_mMinSch1.hap1.2
- File: Miniopterus_schreibersii_original_genome.fna.gz

Part 2 — Assembly Statistics
- Tool: gfastats
- Input file: Miniopterus_schreibersii_original_genome.fna.gz
- Output: Miniopterus_schreibersii_Assembly_Statistics_gfastats
- Main statistics recorded:
  - Total assembly length: 1,850,590,334 bp
  - Number of scaffolds: 186
  - Minimum scaffold length: 13,000 bp
  - Maximum scaffold length: 202,313,579 bp
  - Average scaffold length: 9,949,410.40 bp
  - Scaffold N50: 87,795,433 bp
  - Scaffold L50: 8
  - GC content: 42.51%

Part 3 — Sequence-Length Structure
- Tool: Compute sequence length
- Input file: Miniopterus_schreibersii_original_genome.fna.gz
- Output: Compute sequence length on dataset 1
- The sequence-length results were sorted by length in descending order to identify the five longest sequences.

 Five Longest Sequences
1. NC_138101.1 — 202,313,579 bp
2. NC_138102.1 — 187,805,147 bp
3. NC_138104.1 — 106,815,783 bp
4. NC_138103.1 — 105,355,512 bp
5. NC_138105.1 — 102,193,545 bp

Part 4 — Length-Filtering Experiment
- Step 1: Tool: Filter sequences by length
  - Input file: Miniopterus_schreibersii_original_genome.fna.gz
  - Parameter: minimum length = 10,000 bp (10 kb)
  - Output: Miniopterus_schreibersii_filtered_10kb
- Step 2: Tool: gfastats
  - Input file: Miniopterus_schreibersii_filtered_10kb
  - Same settings as Part 2
  - Output: Miniopterus_schreibersii_Filtered_10kb_Assembly_Statistics_gfastats

Filtering Results

| Metric | Original Genome | After ≥10 kb Filter |
| Total length | 1,850,590,334 bp | 1,850,590,334 bp |
| Number of sequences | 186 | 186 |
| Maximum length | 202,313,579 bp | 202,313,579 bp |
| N50 | 87,795,433 bp | 87,795,433 bp |
| GC content | 42.51% | 42.51% |
No sequences were removed because the shortest scaffold was already 13,000 bp, which is above the 10 kb cutoff.

Part 5 — Small ORF Exploration
- Step 1: Tool: Filter sequences by ID from a tabular file
  - Input file: Miniopterus_schreibersii_original_genome.fna.gz
  - Selected sequence ID: NW_027669791.1
  - Sequence length: 190,730 bp
  - Output: selected sequence for ORF analysis
- Step 2: Tool: getorf
  - Input: selected NW_027669791.1 sequence
  - Minimum nucleotide size of ORF to report: 300 bp
  - Output: Translation of regions between STOP codons
  - All START codons to code for Methionine: Yes
  - Circular sequence: No
  - Output: Miniopterus_schreibersii_getorf.fasta

ORF Results
- Number of ORFs found: 76
- Longest ORF: 97,671 bp
- Longest ORF ID: NW_027669791.1_26
- Coordinates: 32,372–130,042


The Miniopterus schreibersii genome assembly has a total length of about 1.85 Gb and consists of 186 scaffolds. The N50 of 87.8 Mb and L50 of 8 indicate that much of the assembly is contained in a few long scaffolds, although shorter scaffolds are also present. The GC content is 42.51%. The 10 kb filtering experiment did not change the assembly statistics because all scaffolds were already at least 13 kb long. The ORF exploration identified 76 possible ORFs, with the longest being 97,671 bp, but these ORFs cannot automatically be considered real genes without additional evidence.
